WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:03.402
- You need to give away your citizenship.

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:06.638
(patriotic music)

00:00:06.638 --> 00:00:08.679
- Today, I'm taking the
U.S. citizenship test.

00:00:08.679 --> 00:00:10.466
- I'm not sure if I'm gonna pass.

00:00:10.466 --> 00:00:13.386
- I sold my soul to AP
U.S. History for two years,

00:00:13.386 --> 00:00:16.219
so I'm really hoping that I pass.

00:00:22.825 --> 00:00:26.587
- So, I got naturalized
on September 24th, 2015.

00:00:26.587 --> 00:00:28.282
I came from Taiwan.

00:00:28.282 --> 00:00:31.353
- I moved here when I
was about 12 from India.

00:00:31.353 --> 00:00:35.520
- I became an American citizen
in April 15th, last year.

00:00:36.392 --> 00:00:38.667
And I am originally from
the Dominican Republic.

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.525
- So, when you took the test you couldn't,

00:00:40.525 --> 00:00:41.680
you know, answer on paper?

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:42.748
- Oh my gosh
- This is not

00:00:42.748 --> 00:00:44.762
- an open book question, you just have to

00:00:44.762 --> 00:00:46.736
answer the question right there.

00:00:46.736 --> 00:00:49.197
- Right there. Business.

00:00:49.197 --> 00:00:50.579
- I think this test is easy.

00:00:50.579 --> 00:00:54.079
- I took this test and I
passed with very good grades.

00:00:54.079 --> 00:00:56.906
- I did grow up taking American history,

00:00:56.906 --> 00:00:59.780
but I definitely did fresh
up on things before I went,

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.556
'cause I wanted to make sure I passed.

00:01:01.556 --> 00:01:02.827
I think the test is easy.

00:01:02.827 --> 00:01:03.994
- Oh goodness.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.124
- I think I could do well on this.

00:01:06.124 --> 00:01:09.021
- I think I know some about
American history and government.

00:01:09.021 --> 00:01:10.716
- I think I know a good amount.

00:01:10.716 --> 00:01:12.492
I'm not gonna say I'm an expert.

00:01:12.492 --> 00:01:13.416
- Good luck.

00:01:13.416 --> 00:01:14.495
- Thanks, I'm gonna need it.

00:01:14.495 --> 00:01:15.328
- What is the name of the Speaker

00:01:15.328 --> 00:01:18.074
of the House of Representatives now?

00:01:18.074 --> 00:01:19.545
- It's a guy that I don't like,

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:21.002
but some people think he's cute.

00:01:21.002 --> 00:01:22.778
- I don't know any good-looking
guys in the White House.

00:01:22.778 --> 00:01:23.800
- Is it Mitch McConnell? (buzzer)

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:24.805
- Paul Ryan. (bell dinging)

00:01:24.805 --> 00:01:25.900
- I don't know who that is.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:28.321
- Name two National U.S. Holidays.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.790
- Independence day. (bell dinging)

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:31.015
- Martin Luther King
Jr. Day? (bell dinging)

00:01:31.015 --> 00:01:31.848
- Christmas (bell dinging)
and Halloween. (buzzer)

00:01:31.848 --> 00:01:36.204
- Halloween is definitely
not a U.S. holiday.

00:01:36.204 --> 00:01:37.423
- I don't know why I said that.

00:01:37.423 --> 00:01:38.496
I panicked.

00:01:38.496 --> 00:01:41.243
- When was the Declaration
of Independence adopted?

00:01:41.243 --> 00:01:42.799
- I'm like scared, because I know

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:44.093
the general numbers for this

00:01:44.093 --> 00:01:45.556
- You know it, you know it!
- I know a ton of odd numbers

00:01:45.556 --> 00:01:47.077
- in it and it's four digits.

00:01:47.077 --> 00:01:48.243
- July fourth, 1776. (bell dings)

00:01:48.243 --> 00:01:49.076
- Yeah.

00:01:50.263 --> 00:01:52.680
- 75? (buzzer) Oh no!

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.401
- The House of Representatives
has how many voting members?

00:01:55.401 --> 00:01:57.303
- I feel like I know this.

00:01:57.303 --> 00:01:58.168
- Glasses are fogging.

00:01:58.168 --> 00:01:59.997
I'm getting nervous.

00:01:59.997 --> 00:02:00.879
- 300. (buzzer)

00:02:00.879 --> 00:02:01.860
- That times a million is how much money

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.352
I want in my bank account.

00:02:03.352 --> 00:02:05.250
- 500. (buzzer)
- Alright.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.532
- I'm gonna say 50. (buzzer)

00:02:07.532 --> 00:02:10.428
- Is it gonna be like 435? (bell dings)

00:02:10.428 --> 00:02:12.495
- Are you kidding me?

00:02:12.495 --> 00:02:14.701
- Let's go! 3rd grade!

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.169
- Mrs. Murphy!
- Oh my god!

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:18.320
- This many people vote and yet we have

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.397
- Who is the Chief Justice
of the United States now?

00:02:22.397 --> 00:02:25.161
- Chief Justice Sotomayor? (buzzer)

00:02:25.161 --> 00:02:27.540
- They're probably like old and
white and male. (bell dings)

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.771
- It's John Roberts.

00:02:28.771 --> 00:02:31.272
- I wouldn't have known
that, so I'm not upset.

00:02:31.272 --> 00:02:33.345
- Just tell me a very very white name.

00:02:33.345 --> 00:02:34.465
- A very white name?

00:02:34.465 --> 00:02:35.725
Bob Jones? (buzzer)

00:02:35.725 --> 00:02:39.492
- (laughing) It's kind of close.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.541
- How many U.S. senators are there?

00:02:41.541 --> 00:02:43.022
- I'm gonna say 50 on this one. (buzzer)

00:02:43.022 --> 00:02:44.345
- 52. (buzzer)

00:02:44.345 --> 00:02:47.178
- No wait, because it's two per state

00:02:47.178 --> 00:02:48.369
- Yes.
- And there's 50 states.

00:02:48.369 --> 00:02:49.202
- Yes.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.035
- Crap.

00:02:50.035 --> 00:02:52.760
- Who was president during World War I?

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.317
- Wait actually there were two Roosevelts,

00:02:54.317 --> 00:02:55.269
so I guess Roosevelt? (buzzer)

00:02:55.269 --> 00:02:56.102
- Did you know this?

00:02:56.102 --> 00:02:56.935
- Yes.

00:02:56.935 --> 00:02:58.601
- You got it right? Wow.

00:02:58.601 --> 00:02:59.434
- Which one?

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:00.560
- Franklin. (buzzer)

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.319
- No, it was not that one.

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:03.207
- It was Teddy?

00:03:03.207 --> 00:03:05.611
- No, na-no. (laughing)

00:03:05.611 --> 00:03:06.446
- Was it Woodrow Wilson? (bell dings)

00:03:06.446 --> 00:03:08.739
- Yay! That was good.

00:03:08.739 --> 00:03:09.766
- It's cause that was a history question,

00:03:09.766 --> 00:03:11.415
the rest are like current events questions

00:03:11.415 --> 00:03:13.203
which I steer so clear of.

00:03:13.203 --> 00:03:14.036
- You passed. (bell dings)

00:03:14.036 --> 00:03:15.908
- Yay. America!

00:03:15.908 --> 00:03:16.877
(buzzer)

00:03:16.877 --> 00:03:17.968
- Give back your passport.

00:03:17.968 --> 00:03:19.460
- What?

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:20.993
- (buzzer) Is Donald Trump gonna see this?

00:03:20.993 --> 00:03:22.908
Am I gonna be deported?

00:03:22.908 --> 00:03:24.429
- The questions that you got wrong were

00:03:24.429 --> 00:03:26.014
about the government, and I thought that

00:03:26.014 --> 00:03:29.073
everyone knew about the government.

00:03:29.073 --> 00:03:30.222
I guess not.

00:03:30.222 --> 00:03:32.550
- I always joke about how I know more

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:36.062
American history than
natural born Americans, so

00:03:36.062 --> 00:03:38.007
- I can't get mad at you.

00:03:38.007 --> 00:03:40.271
- Most of the questions I
got wrong were about people

00:03:40.271 --> 00:03:43.365
who are in the government,
and I'm not as familiar

00:03:43.365 --> 00:03:44.313
as I probably should be with that.

00:03:44.313 --> 00:03:45.146
This is my country.

00:03:45.146 --> 00:03:46.021
I live here.

00:03:46.021 --> 00:03:47.666
- I don't judge myself for missing some

00:03:47.666 --> 00:03:50.093
of the very current
questions, 'cause I think,

00:03:50.093 --> 00:03:52.413
like a lot of people,
I'm trying to pretend

00:03:52.413 --> 00:03:53.883
politics don't exist right now.

00:03:53.883 --> 00:03:56.118
- When I took it, I thought it was easy,

00:03:56.118 --> 00:03:59.317
but only it was easy
because I studied a lot.

00:03:59.317 --> 00:04:01.755
- I guess I'm gonna have to
study up on my U.S. history.

00:04:01.755 --> 00:04:04.239
- And I'm going to try to be
more open to understanding

00:04:04.239 --> 00:04:05.812
and learning about who's
running our country.

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:07.896
- You need to know a
lot to get into America

00:04:07.896 --> 00:04:10.595
and the restrictions are
getting harder and harder.

00:04:10.595 --> 00:04:14.624
I took my citizenship for granted today.

00:04:14.624 --> 00:04:17.457
(patriotic music)

